A PROBLEM:

Although it's not a bug per se, I would say that being able to get
trapped by your pet(s) is a bad "feature".  A recent example (maybe
it's in the spoiler file?) was the following:

	1) You walk down a dead end corridor.
	2) Pet follows into corridor behind you.
	3) Hill orc follows pet into corridor.
	4) Pet kills Hill Orc; corpse now in corridor.
	5) Hill Orc has a cursed item; pet won't cross item.
	6) You are trapped unless your pet dies (assuming you
	   can't teleport).

I encountered a similar problem.  I turned into a werejackal and summoned
help lots of times, thereby giving myself about 20 pets.  I went
down a corridor and couldn't get back out because my jackals wouldn't
move.  I eventually killed enough to get out, but there weren't any
cursed items blocking the way.  They were blocking the corridor
for no apparent reason (tripping all over each other).

A POSSIBLE SOLUTION

Why not add some mechanism whereby you could exchange positions with
your pet?  It's sort of unreasonable to think that you _couldn't_ get a
friendly animal to swap positions with you.  This would solve the whole
problem, and wouldn't introduce any "cheats" I don't think.  How about
^X [direction] exchanges position with the pet in the specified
direction?

Would someone from the dev team care to comment on this?

